Package: covarchimax
Type: Package
Title: Covariate-Dependent Clayton-Archimax Copulas for Spatial Extremes
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("Ziyi", "Zhou", email = "ellen.zy.syuu@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Semiparametric inference for Clayton-Archimax copulas
    (Charpentier, Fougeres, Genest and Neslehova (2014)
    <doi:10.1016/j.jmva.2013.12.013>) whose Pickands dependence function
    may depend on covariates. Implements the moment-based estimator of the
    Clayton generator parameter of Chatelain, Fougeres and Neslehova (2020)
    <doi:10.1214/19-AOS1836> with a delete-one jackknife standard error;
    Pickands-type, Caperaa-Fougeres-Genest-type and maximum-likelihood
    estimators of the Pickands dependence function in arbitrary dimension;
    an identity-link and a logit-link covariate model for the Pickands
    dependence function, fitted pointwise on the unit simplex with
    explicit optimiser diagnostics; model-implied and empirical
    tail-dependence coefficients; a sampler for bivariate Clayton-Archimax
    copulas; a year-block bootstrap; and helpers for non-stationary
    generalized extreme-value margins with cluster-robust (Godambe
    sandwich) standard errors, built on 'extRemes' (Gilleland and Katz
    (2016) <doi:10.18637/jss.v072.i08>).
